        89.0,
        466.0,
        486.0,
        675.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "We found that the dimension of free poly(MPC) in water is independent of the ionic strength of the salt solution.<sup>[25,26]</sup> Poly(MPC) can be regard as a quite unique zwitter-type polyelectrolyte having the independence of intra- and intermolecular interaction of PMPC from the concentration of $\\mathrm { N a C l } . ^ { [ 2 6 ] }$As a result, the thickness of the high-density polyelectrolyte brushes in solution was observed to change very little in salt solution.",
